A||||13||loafer87gt||Need feedback on new company name||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||05-28-2001||12:53 AM||||I am about to break ties with my old architectural firm and go freelancing, and as such have to decide on a name for my company. I can't believe how difficult it is to decide on one! I had been thinking about Morpheus Studios for some time, but then the Matrix came out and all I can think of is Lawrence Fishburne now when I hear the name. Looking for some brainstorming here, some words that are associated with dreams, visions, being precise, any ideas? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||05-28-2001||01:17 AM||||Dreams + Visions + Precise = Imagineering!<P>No wait, that's already taken.n  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Precision Dreams<BR>Visionotics<P>© 2001 by Steve Normington||||reg||1
Z||000002||JSocha||05-28-2001||01:58 AM||||Loafer, your an architect?<P>To bad you weren't down here in ND.  We are working with Anderson, Wade & Witty out of Minot to do the plans for our Bed & Breakfast.<P>My wife and I are in the process and planning stages of converting our unattached (just under 4,000 square feet - Main level - w/14 foot walls) garage into a two story, 5 (maybe 6) bedroom house for a B&B here in Rugby.<P>They are supposedly the best Architecture firm here in ND (higly recommended by contractors), but extremly slow to get anything accomplished as far as plans.  Any advise to a fellow Fiero owner and Canook  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||05-28-2001||09:12 AM||||Not because it is Fiero related,but I've always looked at Pegasus as flying into the future.How about Pegasus Architechture<BR>(Leading the way)?||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||05-28-2001||03:38 PM||||When I was trying to come up with a name for my graphics business, I made a list of all the cool words I could think of, and started matching them up.. one of the first combinations I came up with was "Digital Fusion", and I liked it, so that's what I went with..<P>if all else fails, try making a list of words and matching them up with words like "design", "architecture", etc.. I bet you'll come up with an awesome name!<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000005||loafer87gt||05-28-2001||03:46 PM||||JSocha: I am afraid I'm not an architect myself. What I do is work with architectural firms to do different massing and design studies, working with them to create computer generated models of their buildings .I can't say I'm familiar with any firms south of the border, so I can't really recommend anyone to you for you renovation. I will ask my Dad, who is an architect, if he has an advice for you however. <BR> <BR> I was brainstorming last night and I came up with something that I think has a nice ring to it. "Ideate Studios" Ideate means to produce from ideas, and that is essentially what I do at work. I don't want to have architecture as part of the title as I don't want to confine myself to that field of work. I figure studio is a bit more broad, and would let me get into some other areas such as archeological visualization and entertainment that I have always wanted to get into. So what do you guys think of think of the name?<p>[This message has been edited by loafer87gt (edited 05-28-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||hugh||05-28-2001||04:04 PM||||So few people know what Ideate means that I wouldn't use it for that reason.Why not just"Idea Studios"<p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 05-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||05-28-2001||07:48 PM||||Sounds a little too much like "Idiot" too me.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever2||05-29-2001||12:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> I've always looked at Pegasus as flying into the future.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Looks like that may be part of the Parts Relay monicker.  Pegasus Fiero Parts Relay is the only name submitted so far.  I like it because it's a Pony Express for the new millennium.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||05-29-2001||06:36 PM||||How about "VD Studios" (Visualization/Design Studios)?<P><BR>Then again, maybe not...<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Robert||05-29-2001||07:14 PM||||About 8 years ago, we started a printing company.  We struggled with the name for weeks.  Our business is in Walnut Creek, Ca.   One day I decided to check if anyone had the name Walnut Creek Printing Company.  Nobody had it.   We got it the same day.  When people need printing in Walnut Creek, where else are they going to go but Walnut Creek Printing?  Customers are always saying what a great name we have there.  It gives the customer a feeling that we have been here forever.<BR>Just an idea;  Saskatoon Architectural Design<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000011||hugh||05-29-2001||07:56 PM||||I think Robert's idea sounded good.||||reg||1
Z||000012||StuGood||05-30-2001||11:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Robert:<BR><B>...Just an idea;  Saskatoon Architectural Design..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>...the only thing I don't care for, is that the acronym, SAD, sounds a little depressing. <P>||||reg||5
Z||000013||loafer87gt||05-31-2001||03:55 AM||||Thanks for the ideas guys. Thanks a lot Stimpy, now I think idiot everytime I hear Ideate as well. LOL. I'm gonna think it over for a coupole more weeks before I register the company, I just need a weekend, when I have some spare time to do some brainstorming. Once again, thanks for suggestions||||reg||1
